      "@type": "Dataset",
      "name": "Long-Distance Move Operations",
      "description": "Long-distance move operations from survey to walkthrough, in eight steps. Survey and quote: a room-by-room survey in person or through the free film-only video walkthrough survey room, where the customer films and a person makes the estimate — nothing is auto-priced — and one flat price agreed in writing before the truck rolls. Inventory: itemized, room by room (published process education: items worth more than $100 per pound are declared in writing under the federal high-value rule — a domain standard, labeled as such). Pack: full or partial packing with furniture fully covered, cross-referenced to the packing category and the interstate pack guide. Load: sequenced loading with blanket and stretch wrap protection; where a move includes a high-mass piece of 1,500 to 3,500 lbs, that piece moves under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation with the KIM-GS Protocol and L/360 floor-deflection analysis. Linehaul: transport along the published I-81, I-66 and I-70 corridor dispatch network from both branches (domain practice, labeled: certified scale weights and consolidated or exclusive-use routing shape the run). Delivery: handled inside a delivery window — the window models are published as domain education in the delivery windows dataset; no company delivery spread, date, or tracking practice is published. Placement: room-by-room placement on the residential pattern, cross-referenced. Walkthrough and claims: a final walkthrough with damage noted on the delivery paperwork, and the valuation level governing any claim — domain education, with no company claims procedure published. Shipment size sets the linehaul inputs (distance bands dataset), the delivery step uses a window model (delivery windows dataset), and the quote step rests on the estimate terms explained in the commercial terms dataset.",
